\section{Geometric Framework}
The TCCM geometry is defined by the extended metric:
\[
ds^2 = g_{\mu\nu} dx^\mu dx^\nu + \Psi^2 d\xi^2,
\]
where $\Psi$ is the chiral twist scalar and $d\xi$ is the chiral
coordinate. The stress-energy tensor is:
\[
\Xi_{\mu\nu}(\Psi),
\]
and the manifold's topology is characterized by Betti numbers
$(\beta_0, \beta_1, \beta_2)$.

These structures allow the manifold to undergo extreme deformation
without singularity formation, supported by active clamping behavior
within the metric kernel.

